# Quickstart

Start the generated service locally and inspect its two public infrastructure endpoints.

## Run

```bash
cp .env.example .env
uv lock
uv sync --locked
make run
```

Local development may bind the loopback HTTP server. Production access requires HTTPS/TLS and
must not expose this development listener directly.

## Root

```bash
curl --fail-with-body http://127.0.0.1:8000/
```

```json
{
  "ok": true,
  "result": null,
  "error": null,
  "error_message": null,
  "retry_after": null
}
```

## OpenAPI

```bash
curl --fail-with-body http://127.0.0.1:8000/getOpenApi
```

The response wraps the unmodified FastAPI OpenAPI document in `PokerlostResponse`. The document
contains no project extension or misleading header-oriented security scheme.

The pristine service exposes no business operation. Before adding one, read
`docs/api/operation-contract.md`, `docs/api/body-authorization.md`, and
`docs/api/pokerlost-response.md`.
